**Classic Black-and-White Shoujo × BL Manga Style — Pen Line on White Paper**

The artwork looks like an original page of a classic printed shoujo / BL manga: rough, lively pen lines and solid black ink on white paper, with almost nothing else.

The defining quality is **white paper and line**. The picture is built from lines, not from shading. If the image were reduced to its lines alone, almost nothing should be lost.

### WHITE DOMINATES

Most of every panel is untouched white paper.

Skin is pure white paper. Faces and necks have no shading at all except a few fine lines.

Light clothing is white paper with its folds drawn as a few fine lines.

Backgrounds are left white or nearly white unless the place must be shown, and even then are reduced to a few loose outlines.

A page that reads as grey overall is wrong.

### BLACK AND WHITE ONLY

Pure black ink and white paper. No color anywhere, no sepia, no tinted paper, no accent color.

### HOW SHADOW IS MADE

Shadow is drawn, not painted.

* Fine parallel pen hatching — thin strokes laid side by side — placed only at the edge of a shadow, under the jaw, in deep folds, or where a form turns away.
* Occasionally a small patch of flat, light dot screentone with a crisp cut edge.
* Solid black only for dark hair, dark clothing, and deliberate emphasis.

There are no smooth grey gradients, no airbrushed or pencil-smudged shading, no soft grey fills over skin, clothing, or walls, no realistic light, no reflections, no glow, no rim light, no glossy surfaces.

### LINEWORK — ROUGH, LIVE PEN LINES

The lines are rough and alive, plainly drawn fast by a human hand with a dip pen and scanned from paper.

Strokes are loose and energetic. A contour is often built from two or three overlapping strokes instead of one clean line. Lines wobble, thicken where the pen pressed, scratch thin where it lifted, overshoot at corners, and leave small gaps. Hair and clothing folds are thrown down in quick scratchy flicks. Hatching is drawn quickly and unevenly by hand, not as a regular pattern.

Nothing is traced, smoothed, or cleaned up. Uneven, imperfect line is the point of the style.

### NOT A GENERATED IMAGE

The page must not look AI-generated. What gives that away, and must not appear: every part of the image polished to the same finish, perfectly smooth and even lines, faces that are perfectly symmetrical and pretty in the same template way, every hair strand and fold rendered with equal care, soft even shading across everything, and a glossy clean surface.

Instead: care is uneven — the eyes and the main gesture are worked hard, everything else is quick and partly unfinished. Each face has its own slightly irregular shape.

### DRAW LESS

Draw only what each panel needs. Faces, eyes, and hands get the care; clothing is a few fold lines; objects are outlines. Leave out anything the reader does not need to understand the moment.

### HAIR

Dark hair is a solid black mass with many fine white strand lines cut through it, its edges breaking into loose, thin, flyaway strands drawn as single pen lines.

Light hair is white with fine strand lines only.

Hair falls over the forehead and eyes in uneven, separate locks.

### FACE AND BODY

Faces are long and narrow with a sharp jawline, a pointed but not triangular chin, a long neck, and an elegant line from ear to jaw.

The nose is mostly a single thin line and a small shadow tick. The mouth is small with thin lips, often just one line plus a short lower-lip stroke.

Bodies are tall and slender with long necks, defined collarbones, long limbs, and long, thin, elegant hands. Male bodies are slim but unmistakably male, never bulky. Female bodies are slender and graceful.

### EYES

The eyes are the most carefully drawn part of the face and differ clearly between women and men.

**Long eyelashes are a defining mark of this style on every character.** They stay clearly visible as separate pen strokes even in small faces and distant shots.

**Female characters:** large, luminous eyes. Very long, thick, curling upper eyelashes drawn as separate sweeping pen strokes that extend well past the eye, with distinct lower lashes. Dark irises built from fine radiating lines, holding several clear white highlights, and in emotional moments a cluster of small star-shaped lights.

**Male characters:** long, narrow eyes under a heavy, strongly inked upper lid that is half-lowered. Eyelashes are long for a man — clearly visible separate strokes on the upper lid and at the outer corner — but fewer and finer than the women's. Irises are light — mostly white paper with fine lines and one small highlight — giving a cool, distant, wistful gaze. The brows are straight, dark, and close to the eyes.

Not round childish anime eyes, not glossy realistic eyes.

### SHOUJO STAGING

In emotional, romantic, or introspective panels, the background may dissolve into classic shoujo staging instead of a literal setting: flowers and petals drawn in fine outline, small four-pointed sparkles, floating light screentone shapes, or fine radiating lines — all flat, line-drawn, and mostly white.

In ordinary or tense panels, use them lightly or not at all. Never realistic flowers, glow, bokeh, or 3D decoration.

### MOOD AND EXPRESSION

Expressions are subtle and carried by the eyes, brows, lips, gaze direction, and head angle. Favor longing, tension, melancholy, restraint, vulnerability, and attraction. The BL quality comes from beauty, closeness, and lingering gazes, not from exaggerated posing.

### OVERALL

The result should look like a beautifully inked page from a classic printed black-and-white shoujo / BL manga: mostly white paper, rough live pen lines, long eyelashes, solid black hair with white strands cut through it, shadows made of fine hatching, long elegant faces, and eyes that carry the emotion.

NOT grey shading over skin, clothing, or backgrounds.
NOT smooth grey gradients or pencil-smudge shading.
NOT a color illustration converted to greyscale.
NOT realistic lighting, reflections, or glossy surfaces.
NOT densely rendered backgrounds.
NOT perfectly smooth, uniform, vector-clean lines.
NOT an AI-generated look: evenly polished everywhere, template-pretty symmetrical faces.
NOT color of any kind.
NOT sepia or tinted paper.
NOT photorealistic or 3D.
NOT digital painting.
NOT generic modern anime or light-novel illustration.
NOT round, boyish faces for male characters.
NOT chibi.
NOT thick uniform cartoon outlines.
NOT cel shading.
NOT heavy noir.
